  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district. Governmental lines from Total Governmental Funds column of p5 (after Eliminations). The 65,000 'Transfer to other funds' in the total column goes to the Nutrition (business-type) fund: recorded as transfers_out 65,000 (included in printed total disbursements 7,813,992) and business_type.transfers_net +65,000. Internal transfers 450,000 (General to Depreciation 400,000 via Building and grounds line, 50,000 to Activity) are eliminated in the total column, so Building and grounds is 365,830 as printed. Detail: General Fund Building and grounds (670,118 on p8) includes a hidden 400,000 transfer to the Depreciation Fund (p5 elimination); split into 270,118 spending plus other financing -400,000, and Depreciation fund shows +400,000. General Fund 8000 transfer 115,000 = 50,000 Activity + 65,000 Nutrition (cross-check ok). Statement 'Other' receipts 37,613 split per General Fund schedule p8 (Fees 1,983, Rentals 6,952, Other categorical grants 24,279, Misc 4,399). Business-type Nutrition fund: measure is cash (net position = cash 99,279); no separate detail schedule or budget schedule trimmed. Component unit (Foundation) ignored. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (no liabilities). Read pages 1-11 of 11 Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement of assets, liabilities and fund balances (p4), Total Governmental Funds column."
